  "description": "BIXZAL crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H95 I20 O25 Tb5,5(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.542-5.108 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.75-159.90°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C150H95I20O25Tb5·5(C7H8). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
